<title>UK: NWE jet slips with gas oil, slack demand.</title>
<headline>NWE jet slips with gas oil, slack demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel markets stayed under pressure on Tuesday from slack demand and lower gas oil prices, traders said.</p>
<p>November IPE November futures fell 50 cents to $208.75 per tonne.</p>
<p>Barges were still valued around Nov IPE +31 fob ARA, although buyers were increasingly basing their bids off the December. Cargo buyers were seen at Dec IPE +26 cif NWE. -- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
